{#-
  ════════ REAL-ESTATE SERIES STRIP ════════

  The real-estate decision, one question per page, with the current page
  marked (PR 8; REAL_ESTATE_PAIR_DESIGN.md §11, rulings P9). Rendered at the
  TOP of each page in the series. The retirement strip followed it there
  on 2026-10-02 (SITE_GUIDE §53.1); it had sat at the foot of its spokes.

  Built on components/retirement-family.njk's pattern: its own scoped
  `<style>`, every selector prefixed `rser-`, every colour a var with a
  literal fallback (the host pages declare their palettes independently),
  one include line per page, and the strip owns its heading, so a host page
  must not wrap it in one:
      {% include 'components/real-estate-series.njk' %}
  Heading level: `{% set rser_level = 'h3' %}` first, if a page needs it.

  THE LINKS CARRY THE SHARED INPUTS (P3). The retirement strip's hrefs are
  plain and can't carry state. Here each link to another page has
  `data-re-carry` (its path) and `data-re-carry-hash` (the calculator), and
  shared/real-estate-carry.js rewrites its href with the page's current
  pair params on load and after any input change. Without script the plain
  href stands. The current page is marked from the page's `slug`.

  MORE SPOKES. Further entries in `series` below, each with the hash its
  calculator answers to. The row takes any number of items.

  THE HUB (2026-10-02, SITE_GUIDE §60). At four spokes the series got the
  retirement family's treatment (§53): a hub at /bitcoin-and-real-estate.
  Three variants, by slug and flag, mirroring retirement-family.njk:
    · on a spoke, the title is a LINK to the hub and the lede ends with
      "All four in one place →";
    · on the hub itself (slug 'bitcoin-and-real-estate') neither link is
      drawn: the H1 a few hundred pixels above already says where you are;
    · on the homepage (`{% set rser_home = true %}` before the include) the
      strip is a section, not a boxed object: no frame, a top hairline,
      centred eyebrow + heading + one-line lede carrying the hub link, on
      the hero's 64rem column. Same Treatment A as `.rfam--home` (§53.1).
-#}
{%- set rserLevel = rser_level | default('h2') -%}
{%- set rserHub = (slug == 'bitcoin-and-real-estate') -%}
{%- set rserHome = (rser_home == true) -%}
<style>
.rser { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(224,148,34,0.09); border-radius: 10px; }
.rser-title { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 0.64rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber, #e09422); margin: 0 0 0.2rem; line-height: 1.4; }
.rser-lede { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-dim, #9a9080); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; max-width: 68ch; }
.rser-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 0.55rem; }
.rser-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 7px; border: 1px solid var(--border-faint, rgba(224,148,34,0.15)); background: rgba(224,148,34,0.035); text-decoration: none; transition: border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s; }
a.rser-item:hover, a.rser-item:focus-visible { border-color: rgba(224,148,34,0.34); background: rgba(224,148,34,0.08); }
.rser-item.is-here { border-color: var(--amber, #e09422); background: rgba(224,148,34,0.1); }
.rser-step { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 0.62rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber, #e09422); }
.rser-item.is-here .rser-step::after { content: ' · you are here'; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: none; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-dim, #9a9080); }
.rser-q { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--ink-bright, #f2eee8); }
.rser-t { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--ink-dim, #9a9080); }
a.rser-item .rser-t::after { content: ' \2192'; color: var(--amber, #e09422); }
.rser-title a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
.rser-title a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-style: dotted; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
.rser-lede a, .rser--home .rser-lede a { color: var(--amber, #e09422); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-style: dotted; text-decoration-color: rgba(224,148,34,0.4); text-underline-offset: 2px; white-space: nowrap; }
.rser-lede a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--amber, #e09422); }
/* HOMEPAGE VARIANT (`rser_home`) — the .rfam--home treatment, so the two
   family sections on the homepage read as a pair. */
.rser.rser--home { max-width: 64rem; margin: 2rem auto 2.5rem; padding: 2rem 3rem 0; border: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(247,147,26,0.15); border-radius: 0; text-align: center; }
.rser--home .rser-title { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
.rser--home .rser-head { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: var(--ink-bright, #f2eee8); margin: 0 0 0.45rem; }
.rser--home .rser-head em { font-style: italic; color: var(--amber, #e09422); }
.rser--home .rser-lede { max-width: none; margin: 0 auto 1.1rem; }
.rser--home .rser-row { text-align: left; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
@media (max-width: 860px) { .rser--home .rser-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .rser.rser--home { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 0; } }
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .rser { padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem 0.9rem; } .rser-row, .rser--home .rser-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .rser.rser--home { padding: 1.75rem 1.25rem 0; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  /* tap targets: inline vertical padding, as .rfam (§53.1, 2026-09-21 fix) */
  .rser-lede a { padding: 0.6rem 0; }
}
</style>
{%- set series = [
  { slug: 'bitcoin-vs-real-estate',     step: 'The tenant',   q: 'Buy or rent?',      t: 'Bitcoin vs. Real Estate',     hash: 'calculator' },
  { slug: 'bitcoin-vs-rental-property', step: 'The landlord', q: 'Keep the rental?',  t: 'Bitcoin vs. Rental Property', hash: 'calculator' },
  { slug: 'bitcoin-vs-paying-down-the-mortgage', step: 'The homeowner', q: 'Pay down the mortgage?', t: 'Bitcoin vs. Paying Down the Mortgage', hash: 'calculator' },
  { slug: 'compare-housing-plans', step: 'Two strategies', q: 'Which approach?', t: 'Compare Housing Plans', hash: 'calculator' }
] -%}
{%- if rserHome %}
<nav class="rser rser--home" aria-labelledby="rser-title">
  <p class="rser-title">The real-estate tools</p>
  <{{ rserLevel }} class="rser-head" id="rser-title">Bitcoin or a home? <em>Four chairs</em>, one decision.</{{ rserLevel }}>
  <p class="rser-lede">Each calculator answers one person&rsquo;s question, and your assumptions travel between them &mdash; <a href="/bitcoin-and-real-estate">see all four in one place &rarr;</a></p>
{%- else %}
<nav class="rser" aria-labelledby="rser-title">
  <{{ rserLevel }} class="rser-title" id="rser-title">{% if rserHub %}Bitcoin and real estate{% else %}<a href="/bitcoin-and-real-estate">Bitcoin and real estate</a>{% endif %}</{{ rserLevel }}>
  <p class="rser-lede">One housing decision, seen from each chair: the tenant, the landlord, the homeowner, and two housing strategies side by side. The links carry the inputs the calculators share.{% if not rserHub %} <a href="/bitcoin-and-real-estate">All four in one place &rarr;</a>{% endif %}</p>
{%- endif %}
  <div class="rser-row">
    {%- for f in series -%}
      {%- if f.slug == slug -%}
    <span class="rser-item is-here" aria-current="page">
      <span class="rser-step">{{ f.step }}</span>
      <span class="rser-q">{{ f.q }}</span>
      <span class="rser-t">{{ f.t }}</span>
    </span>
      {%- else -%}
    <a class="rser-item" href="/{{ f.slug }}#{{ f.hash }}" data-re-carry="/{{ f.slug }}" data-re-carry-hash="{{ f.hash }}">
      <span class="rser-step">{{ f.step }}</span>
      <span class="rser-q">{{ f.q }}</span>
      <span class="rser-t">{{ f.t }}</span>
    </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</nav>
